  "title": "CHAPTER 2: GEOGRAPHY OF TELANGANA",
  "order": 2,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "upmrtx1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Location and Area"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Telangana is a landlocked state situated on the Deccan Plateau in southern India.",
        "Godavari and Krishna are the primary river systems draining the state eastward into the Bay of Bengal.",
        "Red soils cover the majority of Telangana's landscape, alongside black cotton soils in the western and northern districts.",
        "The climate is predominantly semi-arid, receiving maximum rainfall during the South-West Monsoon season.",
        "Amrabad and Kawal are the key designated Tiger Reserves protecting the state's wildlife."
      ],
      "id": "8w9bh3m"
    },
